  "outcome": "DIRECT_SUB_OPTIMAL",
  "best_model_id": "PGS001791",
  "confidence": "Moderate",
  "rationale": "Direct-match candidates are present (pulmonary fibrosis and idiopathic pulmonary fibrosis). Among them, PGS001791 is preferred because it targets the most specific aligned endpoint available (idiopathic pulmonary fibrosis, which is a top local heritability match for the target trait in the provided domain knowledge) and uses a genome-wide continuous shrinkage method (PRS-CS-auto) with a very large variant set (910,439), which is structurally favored over sparse/thresholding approaches. PGS001030 is an exact-label pulmonary fibrosis score but comes from a pan-trait UKB sparse framework (snpnet with 51 variants), which the domain knowledge flags as typically underperforming disease-focused alternatives; additionally its high full-model AUROC (0.8015) is not PRS-comparable and its PGS-only metrics are modest (PGS-only AUROC 0.6252; PGS-only R2 0.0142). PGS004695 has strong incidence effect-size evidence (HR 3.78 high vs low PRS quintile) but is a genome-wide-significant 23-SNP score with no PRS-comparable AUC/R2 reported, limiting comparability. Overall confidence is moderated because PGS001791 lacks a reported PGS-only AUROC (only a covariates-regressed-out R2 is shown) and because the best candidate is for idiopathic pulmonary fibrosis rather than the broader pulmonary fibrosis label."
}

